Panfrost (Bifrost v7): fix overdraw_alpha inversion, opaque blend mode, and
fbfetch destination-load / blend handling on Mali-G52.

1. Fix upstream Mesa 26.2.6 bug in panfrost_overdraw_alpha() (pan_cmdstream.h):
   !info.enabled was inverted and pan_cmdstream.c passed 0/1 swapped for
   overdraw_alpha0/overdraw_alpha1, causing opaque draws to advertise
   overdraw_alpha0 = true.
2. On Bifrost (PAN_ARCH <= 7), use MALI_BLEND_MODE_FIXED_FUNCTION instead of
   MALI_BLEND_MODE_OPAQUE (controlled by PAN_BIFROST_NO_OPAQUE, default on) and
   apply the RGB1->RGBA workaround uniformly.
3. On Bifrost (PAN_ARCH <= 7), set load_destination when the fragment shader
   reads that render target via framebuffer fetch (outputs_read, controlled by
   PAN_BIFROST_FBFETCH_LOADDEST, default on), and provide runtime diagnostic
   toggles PAN_BIFROST_NO_FPK=1 and PAN_BIFROST_FBFETCH_SRCOVER=1.

